spec dd05-unique-under-open-duplicate-rollback: 2 sessions, 3 permutations
# DD05 (G9), rollback arm. 1 101 :K nodes, one with k = 'a'. s1 opens and creates a
# second k = 'a'; s2 creates a UNIQUE constraint on (:K).k in an autocommit statement.
# No committed state may violate the constraint: either the DDL is refused (the
# duplicate committed first) or s1 is (its statement after the DDL, or its COMMIT
# straddling it). The backfill and the value-set must read a committed state, so
# s1's uncommitted duplicate never refuses the DDL.

starting permutation: s1w s1rb s2ddl
step s1w: CREATE (n:K {k:'a', v:'dup'}) RETURN n.k AS k
k  
---
"a"
(1 row)
step s1rb: ROLLBACK
step s2ddl: CREATE CONSTRAINT k_unique FOR (n:K) REQUIRE n.k IS UNIQUE
final fa: MATCH (n:K {k:'a'}) RETURN n.v AS v ORDER BY v
v     
------
"orig"
(1 row)
final fseek: MATCH (n:K {k:'a'}) WITH count(n) AS seek OPTIONAL MATCH (m:K) WHERE m.k + '' = 'a' RETURN seek, count(m) AS scan
seek|scan
----+----
1   |1   
(1 row)
final fschema: <schema>
kind      |name       |definition   
----------+-----------+-------------
index     |__uniq__K.k|             
constraint|k_unique   |UNIQUE (:K).k
(2 rows)

